# Environment / secrets
.env
*.env
# ...except the two committed example configs. Both are part of the checkout - the
# run configurations use them and docs/adr/0004 refers to them - so they must be
# re-included, or a fresh `git add -A` would silently leave them behind.
!tests/.env
!docs/.env

# Private working notes, none of them part of the published project. CLAUDE.md and
# TODO.md are working documents; RELEASE_PLAN_1.0.md additionally records what this
# repository's history contains, so it must never reach the public repository.
CLAUDE.md
TODO.md
RELEASE_PLAN_1.0.md

# Personal working files - carry identifying business information. The canonical,
# placeholder-only template ships in time_tracker_templates/.
LPC *.xlsx

# Real invoices and time logs written by a default (relative) configuration. Named
# precisely rather than by filename pattern, so the deliberately tracked
# docs/Invoice 10* examples are not caught by them.
/invoices/
/time_logs/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.venv/
.venv_laptop/

# Coverage
.coverage
htmlcov/

# IDE
.idea/
*.swp

# Generated test invoices, and whatever a test run writes into the log directory.
# The one committed time log is the working copy the manual run configurations use;
# restore_test_data.sh copies it back from tests/bak after a run has edited it, so
# it has to be in the checkout for that to have anywhere to restore to.
tests/data/*.pdf
tests/data/*.xlsx
tests/data/time_logs/*
!tests/data/time_logs/test_time_log.csv

# Build / dist
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Bak directories
bak/

# ...except tests/bak, which is not scratch: it holds the pristine fixtures that
# tests/restore_test_data.sh copies back into tests/data. Both rules are needed -
# the first re-includes the directory, which git would otherwise never look
# inside, and the second its contents. Compiled bytecode stays ignored, since the
# re-include would otherwise beat the __pycache__ rule above (last match wins).
!tests/bak/
!tests/bak/**
tests/bak/__pycache__/

# Backups written by tools/repair_template_external_links.py
*.xlsx.bak
